(null, null, null, timestamptz '2026-09-18 00:00:00+00', 'research-agent-group-c', 1, 'unresolved',
 'GAP IA/MD/ce_topic_abuse_reporter_hours -- AND A VOCABULARY GAP. Iowa DIAL states that physicians in certain specialties must, at audit, submit "a copy of the certificate showing completion of the training within the last five years" for abuse identification and reporting. A FIVE-YEAR RECURRING TRAINING IS VERIFIED; the HOUR COUNT IS NOT, and the permitted topic names (opioid, ethics, implicit_bias, human_trafficking, medical_errors, domestic_violence, hiv_aids, pain_management, controlled_substance, laws_and_rules, jurisprudence_ethics, impairment, pharmacotherapeutics) contain no abuse-reporter slot. domestic_violence is the nearest name and is NOT the same subject -- Iowa''s duty is mandatory-reporter training for child and dependent adult abuse. NOT SEEDED under any key. OPEN: read IAC 481 ch. 654 for the hour count and add a ce_topic_mandatory_reporter_hours key. Source: https://dial.iowa.gov/licenses/health-professions/physicians/continuing-education-physicians'),

(null, null, null, timestamptz '2026-09-18 00:00:00+00', 'research-agent-group-c', 1, 'unresolved',
 'QUALIFIER ON THE IOWA END-OF-LIFE ROW: it is seeded under ce_topic_pain_management_hours because the vocabulary has no end-of-life-care name, and its value_json carries "topic": "end-of-life care" so the mismatch is visible in the data rather than only here. Iowa has TWO separate five-year topic duties -- two hours on the CDC opioid-prescribing guideline (seeded under ce_topic_opioid_hours) and two hours on end-of-life care (seeded under ce_topic_pain_management_hours) -- with different trigger populations. A consumer that reads only the key names will think Iowa has a pain-management requirement it does not have. OPEN: add a ce_topic_end_of_life_hours key. Source: https://dial.iowa.gov/chronic-pain-and-end-life-training'),

(null, null, null, timestamptz '2026-09-18 00:00:00+00', 'research-agent-group-c', 1, 'unresolved',
 'GAP IA/APRN/supervision_required and IA/APRN/collaborative_agreement_required. Iowa Administrative Code 655 ch. 7 was read in full and states "An ARNP licensed by the board may prescribe, administer, or dispense prescription drugs or devices, including controlled substances, within the ARNP''s role and population foci" -- with no collaboration or supervision condition attached. The chapter defines "collaboration" but requires it only in the fluoroscopy-supervision context. IOWA IS ALMOST CERTAINLY A FULL-PRACTICE-AUTHORITY STATE, and a false on both keys would probably be right -- but the board asserts the POSITIVE grant, not the negative of a requirement, and this table does not convert an absence into a false. NOT SEEDED. OPEN: obtain an affirmative DIAL or Board statement that no collaborative agreement is required, then seed both as false. THIS IS A HIGH-VALUE, LOW-EFFORT OPEN ITEM. Source: https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/05-28-2025.655.7.pdf'),

