(null, null, null, timestamptz '2026-09-18 00:00:00+00', 'research-agent-group-c', 1, 'unresolved',
 'GAP MO/MD/renewal_cycle_months -- THE SINGLE MOST CONSEQUENTIAL MISSING VALUE IN GROUP C. Missouri''s physician CME is verified at 50 hours over a FIXED 24-month calendar window ("beginning January 1 of each even-numbered year and ending December 31 of each odd-numbered year", 20 CSR 2150-2.125), and the fee rule 20 CSR 2150-2.080 gives a single "Renewal Fee $147" without stating a period. THE CME PERIOD IS NOT NECESSARILY THE LICENCE PERIOD, and in this very group Minnesota proves they can differ by a factor of three. RSMo 334.075 was read and addresses only the CE condition on renewal, not the frequency; revisor.mo.gov then refused further automated access ("appears a bot-like access pattern was detected") so RSMo 334.071 could not be read, and pr.mo.gov''s Healing Arts and Physicians and Surgeons pages publish MOPRO account guidance rather than the renewal cycle. NOT SEEDED. Deriving 24 months from the CME window would be the exact failure mode this asset exists to prevent. OPEN: read RSMo 334.071 and 20 CSR 2150-2.010 by hand.'),

(null, null, null, timestamptz '2026-09-18 00:00:00+00', 'research-agent-group-c', 1, 'unresolved',
