(null, null, null, timestamptz '2026-09-18 00:00:00+00', 'research-agent-group-c', 1, 'unresolved',
 'KANSAS IS THE SPARSEST STATE IN GROUP C AND DELIBERATELY SO. GAP KS/MD for EVERY field_key: renewal_cycle_months, renewal_window_days, ce_hours_total, ce_cycle_months, every ce_topic key, initial_license_fee_cents, renewal_fee_cents, fingerprint_required, csr_required. Four Kansas Board of Healing Arts pages were read on 2026-09-18 -- Renewal Dates, the Doctor of Medicine and Surgery licensing FAQ, the Doctor of Medicine and Surgery licence-type page, and the General Counsel Healing Arts FAQ -- and NONE of them publishes an hour count, a fee, or a cycle length. The Renewal Dates page gives a renewal PERIOD of "May 15 - July 31" for "MD, MD Resident Active" with late renewal "July 1 - July 31"; that is a pair of calendar dates, not a cycle length and not a window in days, and converting it would be invented precision. K.S.A. 65-2809 was read in full and expressly delegates all of it: "The license shall be canceled on the date established by rules and regulations of the board" and "The requirements for continuing education for licensees of each branch of the healing arts shall be established by rules and regulations adopted by the board." The operative K.A.R. 100-15 series is not served in retrievable form from ksbha.ks.gov or ksrevisor.gov. NOT ONE KS/MD ROW IS SEEDED. An honestly empty Kansas is the correct deliverable; a Kansas populated from Nebraska or Missouri would be a defect. OPEN: obtain K.A.R. 100-15-4, 100-15-5 and the Board fee regulation, by hand or by request to the Board.'),

(null, null, null, timestamptz '2026-09-18 00:00:00+00', 'research-agent-group-c', 1, 'unresolved',
